  "verbalization": "Quisqualic acid appears to interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through multiple indirect pathways, suggesting a potential role in regulating the activity of this kinase. The evidence indicates that Quisqualic acid targets 5-oxoprolinase, which in turn is a target of Lactucin, and both of these are involved in targeting PITSLRE CDC2L1. Similarly, Quisqualic acid also targets G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1, which is a target of 2,3,5,8-Tetramethyldecane, and both of these are linked to PITSLRE CDC2L1. These findings suggest that Quisqualic acid may modulate the activity of PITSLRE CDC2L1 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving the regulation of cyclin B1 and other downstream targets. The integration of these pathways implies that Quisqualic acid could influence the kinase activity of PITSLRE CDC2L1 through a network of interconnected targets, potentially affecting cell cycle regulation and other biological processes. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Quisqualic acid and PITSLRE CDC2L1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
